#
# Provides the CMYK struct representing a color in the Cyan-Magenta-Yellow-Key
# subtractive color space used by printers and print media. Unlike the additive
# RGB model where combining colors produces white, CMYK subtracts light from
# white paper. The Key (black) channel is added because mixing cyan, magenta,
# and yellow inks produces a muddy brown rather than true black in practice.
#
# This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
# any later version.
